{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788761044287065001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"trivial-protected-barracuda","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"b32e44150ffadfb266f8d5c9ec934a9d56d7cc338718d6a51909db4d302e7e34","event_uuid":"6d463cf6-542d-4fbb-a497-77f6087d40a8","position":{"commit_sha":"5a24ddf52981ab0bb7332e80623444539278484e","position":"1788753773815803001-6d463cf6-542d-4fbb-a497-77f6087d40a8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"76f69a9a1653d82886e9196d6c6cc5babc77b22320fcf4a874afe023d7fc6764","event_uuid":"79b431f2-e058-4e7e-b4ec-ba3848660744","position":{"commit_sha":"3e7e6992d871e158f5d020a5055325b06ddb1cc4","position":"1788753795329082001-79b431f2-e058-4e7e-b4ec-ba3848660744"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"e8c6592106f8f3d2e99c616ef0215e246ca006a81cf5881308098f2cff7ff8fc","event_uuid":"cbe3e2fe-ab92-4364-a329-188055694a26","position":{"commit_sha":"939ed530a8e5a112dad4ee5cad340b590676adef","position":"1788753811987438001-cbe3e2fe-ab92-4364-a329-188055694a26"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788753773815803001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"79b431f2-e058-4e7e-b4ec-ba3848660744","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"9ea3-7d07-ea55-4496"},{"link_uuid":"cbe3e2fe-ab92-4364-a329-188055694a26","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"9ea3-7d07-ea55-4496"}],"description":"Replacement/residual bug split from witted-invisible-roan after completion verification refused close on 2026-09-07.\n\nResidual defect:\nThe configured rebar MCP endpoint can still return persistent HTTP 502 after concurrent gate load if the MCP process is OOM-killed or otherwise dies while nginx's materialized single-server upstream still points at the dead backend. The parent landed detection, retire-sweep repair, memory instrumentation, and a reduced whole-store read footprint, but those do not prove the serving path cannot recur under concurrent gate load.\n\nVerifier blocker on parent, summarized:\n- nginx still has a single materialized upstream with no failover path;\n- memory oversubscription under concurrent gates is not bounded by admission control, instance sizing, or off-box execution;\n- existing comments identify the latency/read-scan issue (`lousy-unsuited-gnu` / `94c5-b42e-ac80-4f06`) as separate and not fixed by the memory reduction.\n\nDesign question to resolve here:\nChoose the prevention mechanism(s) for recurrence — e.g. MCP upstream failover/self-healing, gate admission/concurrency limits, moving gate execution off-box, or a data-backed capacity change — and implement enough that `/mcp` cannot remain pinned to a dead backend after gate-induced MCP failure.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- [ ] The selected design is recorded with why alternatives were accepted/rejected.\n- [ ] A reproduced or simulated MCP backend death under gate-like load recovers without a persistent nginx 502.\n- [ ] The prevention is covered by tests through the relevant surface(s) and by an operator-visible metric/log/alarm.\n- [ ] Any capacity/concurrency number used by the prevention cites measured data, including or linking the AC5 campaign split to `inherited-americium-porpoise`.\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"85a5-97ff-4a47-4c77","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Prevent persistent MCP 502 recurrence","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["6d463cf6-542d-4fbb-a497-77f6087d40a8","79b431f2-e058-4e7e-b4ec-ba3848660744","cbe3e2fe-ab92-4364-a329-188055694a26"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788761044287065001,"uuid":"39845fb4-e7c9-4e74-bfd2-cd39ed5ef48a"}